SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Treaty on the Prohibition of Nuclear Weapons","publisher":"United Nations Treaty Collection","publication_date":"2022-09-22","url":"https://treaties.un.org/Pages/showDetails.aspx?objid=08000002804c2398","claim":"The UN Treaty Collection lists the Democratic Republic of the Congo as having ratified the TPNW on 22 September 2022, with entry into force for the DRC on 21 December 2022.","locator":"status table, DRC row","source_type":"primary/legal","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Depositary treaty record is authoritative for the ratification date and entry into force.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Direct 2022 treaty act.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate-to-high: this was a formal state act under Tshisekedi's government, though executed through foreign-affairs and cabinet channels.","contrary_evidence":["This is a legal status record, not proof of deeper implementation beyond ratification."],"lenses":["1B.4","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Democratic Republic of the Congo | Treaty on the Prohibition of Nuclear Weapons","publisher":"ICAN","publication_date":"unknown","url":"https://www.icanw.org/drc","claim":"ICAN states that the DRC's council of ministers approved TPNW ratification on 6 May 2022 and that President Tshisekedi signed an ordinance on 15 August 2022 authorizing it.","locator":"Signature and ratification section, lines 68-76","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Secondary source, but the claim is specific and consistent with the UN treaty record on the ratification date.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 process evidence inside the target year.","ruler_attribution":"High for the formal authorization step, because ICAN attributes the ordinance to Tshisekedi personally.","contrary_evidence":["The ordinance detail is not independently verified in this pass."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.4","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Democratic Republic of the Congo | Treaty on the Prohibition of Nuclear Weapons","publisher":"ICAN","publication_date":"unknown","url":"https://www.icanw.org/drc","claim":"ICAN reports that in 2022 the DRC observed the first Meeting of States Parties to the TPNW and said deterrence is a false guarantee of security; it also says the DRC has promoted universal adherence to the treaty by co-sponsoring and consistently voting for the annual UNGA resolution since 2018.","locator":"Meetings of states parties and Article 12 sections, lines 98-104","source_type":"NGO","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"The source quotes and summarizes a public state position, but it is still a campaign NGO account rather than a primary transcript.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"2022 statement with later implementation context.","ruler_attribution":"Moderate: the statement is attributed to the DRC at the treaty meeting, but not directly to Tshisekedi personally.","contrary_evidence":["This is advocacy rhetoric and does not by itself prove operational restraint."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.2","1B.4","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Country List : Office of Legal Affairs : IAEA","publisher":"IAEA","publication_date":"2026-03-23","url":"https://ola.iaea.org/Applications/FactSheets/Country/Detail?code=CD","claim":"The IAEA country sheet lists the DRC's NPT safeguards agreement and its additional protocol as in force, and shows the DRC as party to the Convention on the Physical Protection of Nuclear Material.","locator":"Safeguards Agreements, lines 112-124","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official IAEA status record for safeguards and physical-protection obligations.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Baseline nuclear-safeguards posture in force during 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Low-to-moderate: these are inherited treaty obligations, but they define the non-nuclear baseline under which Tshisekedi governed.","contrary_evidence":["This is a standing status record rather than a 2022 policy act by Tshisekedi."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.4","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"la Stratégie nationale de cybersécurité","publisher":"Presidence RDC","publication_date":"2023-06-23","url":"https://www.presidence.cd/actualite-detail/actualite/la_strategie_nationale_de_cybersecurite","claim":"The presidency says the National Cybersecurity Strategy 2022-2025 was developed by 32 experts under the impulse of President Tshisekedi and validated by him in 2022.","locator":"lines 72-76","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official page gives direct attribution and dates for the strategy's development and validation.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Work was carried out in February-July 2022 and validated inside the target year.","ruler_attribution":"High: the page explicitly ties the strategy to Tshisekedi's impulse and validation.","contrary_evidence":["Official self-report may overstate coherence or eventual execution."],"lenses":["1B.7","1B.9","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Compte rendu de la soixante-treizième réunion du Conseil des Ministres","publisher":"Presidence RDC","publication_date":"2022-10-16","url":"https://presidence.cd/conseil-de-ministres/compte_rendu_de_la_soixante_treizieme_reunion_du_conseil_des_ministres","claim":"The council minutes say Tshisekedi validated the 7-pillar National Cybersecurity Strategy, which had been presented on 14 October 2022, and recommended creating a National Cybersecurity Agency and a legal corpus for cybercrime response.","locator":"lines 98-103","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Official minutes show concrete institutional follow-through, though they still record planned implementation rather than finished results.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Mid-October 2022.","ruler_attribution":"High: the minutes explicitly attribute the validation and instructions to Tshisekedi.","contrary_evidence":["This records adoption and recommendation, not actual agency creation or successful execution."],"lenses":["1B.3","1B.7","1B.9","1B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Adresse à la nation du Président de la République, Félix Tshisekedi suite à la détérioration de la situation sécuritaire à l’est du pays","publisher":"Presidence RDC","publication_date":"2022-11-03","url":"https://presidence.cd/actualite-detail/actualite/adresse_a_la_nation_du_president_de_la_republique_felix_tshisekedi_suite_a_la_deterioration_de_la_situation_securitaire_a_lest_du_pays","claim":"Tshisekedi said the M23 advance had created a humanitarian crisis with more than 200,000 displaced people and ordered the government to gather and care for them.","locator":"line 78","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct presidential address states the crisis scale and the government's response order.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"November 2022 within the target year.","ruler_attribution":"High: the instruction is explicitly issued by the president during an active crisis.","contrary_evidence":["This concerns a conventional armed conflict, not nuclear use."],"lenses":["1B.1","1B.8","1B.10"]}

Search ledger:
- Candidates found: about 30-35 plausible documents across UN treaty records, IAEA, ICAN, Presidency RDC, and Security Council materials.
- Documents opened: 11 accessible documents/pages in this pass.
- Duplicate families removed: 8.
- Irrelevant or out-of-period items: 4.
- Inaccessible items: 3.
- Accepted distinct new URLs: 6.
- Reused URLs already accepted in prior batches: 3.

Material gaps:
- DRC has no nuclear arsenal, so the cleanest 1B evidence is baseline nonproliferation plus limited dual-use/cyber choices, not nuclear command-and-control.
- I did not find a 2022 primary record showing direct presidential control over any nuclear force, because none exists.
- I did not find a 2022 primary or legal record for biological-weapons policy, chemical-weapons operational measures, or a formal article-2 declaration published in 2022; the best available declaration is retrospective in 2023.
- I did not fully exhaust UN meeting transcripts on the DRC's 2022 treaty statements because some UN pages were JS-gated or 404-prone in this environment.

Next best directions if you want a second saturation wave:
1. `UNODA` or `UN meeting records` for the DRC’s 2022 First Committee and TPNW meeting statements, especially full transcripts.
2. `UNTC` / `OPCW` / `UNODA` treaty-status pages for any additional DRC WMD or disarmament actions in 2022.
3. `Code du Numérique`, `Malabo Convention`, and any 2022-2023 implementation follow-up for the cybersecurity strategy.
4. `Security Council` and `MONUSCO` records only if you want to widen the chapter to broader crisis-risk management rather than staying near nuclear/nonproliferation exposure.
